<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23220" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-fit</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. def.</i> (infĭunt, <i><span class="en">Mart.
				Cap. 2, § 220</span></i>: infe <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρξαι,</span> Gloss.: infĭo, Varr.
			ap. <i><span class="en">Prisc. 8 <i>fin.</i></span></i>), <i>he</i> (<i>she</i>, <i>it</i>), <i>begins</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infit me percontarier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 2, 2, 76</span></i>
			: laudare  formam virginis, <i><span class="en">id. Rud.
				prol. 51</span></i>. postulare plorans ejulans, ut, etc., <i><span class="en">id. Aul. 2,
				4, 39</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">commutare animum (with adoritur),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					3, 515</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">erigere caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					5, 1208</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ita farier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 11, 242</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>He begins to speak</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">his vocibus infit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 5, 708</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">talibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10, 860</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tum ita Tullus infit: Romani, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					1, 28, 4</span></i>
			; cf. with acc. and <i>inf.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ibi infit, annum se tertium et octogesimum
					agere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					3, 71, 6</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			gen., <i>he speaks</i>, <i><span class="en">Prud.
				Apoth. 805</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
